        "Make an indoor photographic working portrait of a person guided by the supplied face and hair reference, newly portrayed as a fictional woman in her late twenties, wearing autumn layering. The face has the reference's rounded oval shape, brown eyes, small straight nose and softly shaped lips. Short black bobbed hair and fine forehead bangs follow the reference silhouette. The supplied image guides visible facial appearance and hairstyle. Catch a complex moment of visible cause and effect inside a small textile studio, where she is building a striped scarf on a compact wooden table loom and keeping its edge from drawing inward as the next weft crosses. She sits on a plain wooden chair beside the near end of the loom, hips supported by the seat and both low-heeled shoes resting on the floor. Her torso makes a small forward turn toward the working area. The loom is fixed on a narrow table close to her seated elbow height, offset to her right in the picture, leaving the front of her outfit and her bent trouser legs visible. Its raised rigid heddle separates the taut warp into an upper layer and a lower layer, making a clear passage for the shuttle. Her left thumb and forefinger maintain a small slack loop of pale weft yarn at the left cloth edge, while her right hand receives the wooden boat shuttle as it emerges from the opposite side of the open warp shed. The hands reach two separate edges of the same small loom. A fresh rust-colored stripe lies straight across the woven section nearest her; beyond it, long bare warp threads continue toward the rear beam. The pale yarn trailing from the shuttle curves gently at the near edge rather than pulling the finished stripe inward. Her gaze follows the emerging shuttle, lips slightly parted in quiet concentration, with her face readable in three-quarter view above the work. Her forest-green corduroy overshirt is worn open, its broad vertical wales and stitched patch-pocket edge visible in the window light. Inside it, 